police in new york city and washington  d.c are working with their federal  counterparts to look for a suspect  linked now to multiple shootings of  homeless people in both of those cities  five people overall have been shot since  march third two of those people killed  and last night another homeless person  was found dead in manhattan police are  working to determine the cause of death  and whether that incident is related to  the others but nancy chan has put  together the latest on the investigation  and we should warn you that some of the  images in her report  are disturbing  if you had any kind of interaction in  these areas this morning we strongly  encourage you to please report it  authorities in new york city are  offering a 10 thousand dollar reward to  find this man who they say is  responsible for two shootings on  saturday morning that killed one  homeless man and left another injured  the nypd says the first victim a  38-year-old hispanic male was sleeping  on a corner when a person came up and  shot him in the right arm the victim  then screamed at the suspect as he fled  the victim is recovering in the hospital  less than two hours later police say the  same man seen in this surveillance video  approached a second homeless man also  sleeping on a lower manhattan street  just blocks away the suspect lingers  over the man nudging him a few times  before opening fire striking the  unidentified man in the head and neck  the victim was later pronounced dead at  the scene  those shootings came as the metropolitan  police department in washington on  sunday alleged the suspect's attacks on  homeless men started in their city d.c  police say three homeless individuals  were shot over a period of six days  starting march 3rd one fatally  yesterday the mayors of both new york  and washington d.c released a joint  statement urging all homeless persons to  seek shelter as law enforcement works to  track down what they call a cold-blooded  killer on the loose adding our  communities in d.c and new york city are  heartbroken and disturbed by these  heinous crimes in which an individual  has been targeting some of our most  vulnerable residents  and last night police here in new york  city found another deceased homeless man  this time in the tribeca neighborhood  police say they had warned the victim  earlier in the day that two homeless men  had been attacked here in lower  manhattan the previous night it's not  yet clear if his death is connected to  the other incidents  tony  we got pretty good pictures of the  suspect there i hope someone recognizes  that individual nancy thank you very  much
 

